  "lines": [
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Dad, how do airplanes stay up in the sky?",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "✈️",
          "label": "Airplane"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "☁️",
          "label": "Stay up?"
        },
        "mid": "?"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "It's all about the wings! Planes have big wings that are shaped and tilted just right.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "✈️",
        "text": "It's the wings!",
        "cue": "wings",
        "sub": "Shaped and tilted",
        "sub_cue": "tilted"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "But the wings don't even flap like a bird's."
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "They don't need to! First, big engines push the plane forward, really fast.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "💨",
        "text": "Engines push forward",
        "cue": "engines",
        "sub": "Really fast!",
        "sub_cue": "fast"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "As the plane zooms along, air rushes past the wings. The tilted wings push that air down...",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "Zoom!",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "✈️",
            "label": "The plane zooms",
            "cue": "zooms"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💨",
            "label": "Air rushes past",
            "cue": "rushes"
          },
          {
            "icon": "⬇️",
            "label": "Wings push air down",
            "cue": "down"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "...and the air pushes the wings back up! That upward push is called lift.",
      "punch": "lift",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "⬆️",
        "text": "LIFT!",
        "cue": "lift",
        "sub": "Air pushes the wings up",
        "sub_cue": "upward"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Does a paper airplane have lift too?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Yes! Its paper wings make a little bit of lift. And your throw is its engine!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "📄",
        "text": "Your throw = the engine",
        "cue": "throw",
        "sub": "Paper wings lift too",
        "sub_cue": "wings"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "How does a big plane come back down?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "The pilot slows the engines and tips the nose a little lower, so the plane glides gently down to the runway.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🛬",
        "text": "Slow down, glide down",
        "cue": "glides",
        "sub": "Hello, runway!",
        "sub_cue": "runway"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So the engines push it forward, and the wings lift it up!",
      "board": {
        "type": "summary",
        "rows": [
          {
            "icon": "💨",
            "text": "Engines push",
            "cue": "engines"
          },
          {
            "icon": "✈️",
            "text": "Wings lift",
            "cue": "wings"
          },
          {
            "icon": "⬆️",
            "text": "Up it goes!",
            "cue": "up"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Ready for takeoff! Ask a grown-up to subscribe to The Curio Kids Club for more wonders! And next time someone asks... how do airplanes stay up in the sky?"
    }
